Let's Encrypt's Gen Y RSA intermediates, for NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS in
.github/workflows/update-coffee-stats.yml.

Since its certificate renewal on 2026-10-22, the loyalty portal's API
(loyaltyportal-api.electronicline.com) sends only its own certificate and
leaves out the intermediate. Browsers fetch a missing intermediate
themselves; Node doesn't, so every request failed with
UNABLE_TO_VERIFY_LEAF_SIGNATURE. Root YR isn't in Node's bundled CA store
yet either, so it's included in its form cross-signed by ISRG Root X1, which
is. Trust still ends at ISRG Root X1; nothing here is a new trust anchor.

YR1-YR3 are all here because Let's Encrypt may issue the next renewal from
any of them. They expire 2028-09-02; the cross-signed Root YR, 2032-09-02.

Source: https://letsencrypt.org/certificates/ (int-yr1.pem, int-yr2.pem,
int-yr3.pem, root-yr-by-x1.pem), fetched 2026-10-23.

Delete this file and its workflow line once the API serves its full chain:
  openssl s_client -connect loyaltyportal-api.electronicline.com:443 -showcerts
should list more than one certificate.

